    "question": "What is a correlation ID?",
    "shortAnswer": "An identifier linking events belonging to a request or workflow.",
    "detailedAnswer": "Propagate it across service boundaries and include it in logs. Distributed tracing can additionally represent parent-child spans.\n\nA correlation ID connects log entries belonging to a request across components. Generate or validate an incoming identifier at the service boundary, propagate it through outbound calls and include it in structured logs. For example, checkout, inventory and payment logs can share a request identifier to simplify investigation. In asynchronous Java code, thread-local logging context may need explicit propagation and cleanup. Distributed tracing adds trace and span identifiers to represent causal relationships and timing. Do not use correlation IDs as authentication credentials.",
