    "question": "What is a unit test?",
    "shortAnswer": "A test of a small unit of behavior in isolation.",
    "detailedAnswer": "JUnit supports assertions and test lifecycle management. Mock external dependencies when useful, but test observable behavior rather than implementation details.\n\nA unit test checks a small behavior in isolation, such as verifying that a discount calculator returns the expected amount for a given order. JUnit provides @Test and assertions; mocks or fakes can isolate external dependencies when needed. Use arrange, act and assert to make intent clear, and cover boundary cases and failures as well as successful paths. Tests should be deterministic and fast. Avoid excessive mocking of internal implementation details because harmless refactoring should not break behavior-focused tests.",
    "isPublished": true,
    "detailedAnswerTelugu": "Unit test ఒక చిన్న behavior ను విడిగా పరీక్షిస్తుంది. ఉదాహరణకు DiscountCalculator సరైన discount ఇస్తుందో JUnit @Test మరియు assertEquals తో చూడవచ్చు. Arrange లో input సిద్ధం చేసి Act లో method call చేసి Assert లో result పరిశీలిస్తారు. అవసరమైతే external dependencies కు mocks లేదా fakes వాడాలి. Success, failure, boundary cases పరీక్షించాలి. Internal implementation పై అధికంగా ఆధారపడితే refactoring సమయంలో అనవసరంగా tests fail అవుతాయి."
