    "question": "What is an integration test?",
    "shortAnswer": "A test verifying interactions between components or real dependencies.",
    "detailedAnswer": "It can expose configuration, transaction and serialization issues missed by unit tests. Use controlled test data and reproducible environments.\n\nAn integration test checks interactions between real components, such as a Spring repository executing SQL against a test database. It can detect incorrect mappings, transaction behavior, migrations or configuration that isolated unit tests miss. Testcontainers can provide disposable database instances when a suitable container runtime is available. Keep test data controlled, isolate tests from production services and clean up resources. Integration tests are generally slower than unit tests, so use both in a balanced test suite and run critical end-to-end scenarios separately.",
